{#
  Plan P6-T4: RTL demo, ported from the canonical Svelte reference
  (lily-design-system-svelte-sveltekit-examples/src/routes/rtl-demo/+page.svelte).
  Proves the internationalization design principle in
  AGENTS/internationalization.md -- "components do not assume LTR layout
  in their structural HTML" -- with a real page: dir="rtl" plus real
  Arabic content, using components (breadcrumb, data table, pagination,
  a form with radios/checkboxes) that are the classic places a design
  system silently bakes in "left" instead of "start".

  Deliberate deviation from the Svelte reference: the front-matter
  `title` above stays English ("RTL Demo") because this app's
  layouts/page.njk always renders <h1>{{ title }}</h1> as the page's
  one semantic H1, and every other composed page here (Book an
  Appointment, Page Layout, Dashboard, ...) keeps that title in English
  for site-chrome/tab-title consistency -- the shared header/footer
  chrome around this route is the site's own English chrome, not a
  bespoke Arabic Header/Footer as in the Sveltekit app (which has no
  such shared per-route chrome to begin with). The actual RTL proof --
  everything below, wrapped in dir="rtl" lang="ar" -- is the exact
  Arabic content from the canonical reference, byte-for-byte.

  Unlike the Svelte reference (whose own per-app nhs.css turned out to
  be dead code, with real styling coming entirely from the runtime
  theme), THIS app's src/assets/css/ is fully live, and -- being
  entirely unlayered -- always beats the runtime theme's `@layer lily`
  rules regardless of specificity (the same mechanism reset.css's own
  comment already documents for the button/input reset). So the
  shared theme already using logical properties (text-align: start,
  border-inline-start, ...) did NOT make this route correct on its
  own: this app's own component CSS -- data-table(-th/-td), the
  breadcrumb separator, inset-text's border, and radio/checkbox
  spacing, plus the ol/ul indent in reset.css -- had real,
  previously-undiscovered physical-property bugs (text-align: left,
  padding-left, margin-right, border-left), caught by this route's
  first live e2e run (a genuine test failure: computed textAlign was
  "left" instead of "start") and fixed in place. Left deliberately
  unfixed, matching the reference's own "honest note, not a full
  audit" restraint: the same pattern elsewhere in files this route
  doesn't exercise (table-th.css, calendar-/kanban-/gantt-table-*,
  field.css's invalid-state rule, back-link.css's chevron direction).
#}

